    {
      "id": "create-a85f7d",
      "name": "Create",
      "category": "pointer",
      "signature": "Create(Target, Root, Allocator, Already Exist)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "GenericPointer*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Root",
          "type": "ValueType&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Allocator",
          "type": "ValueType::AllocatorType&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Already Exist",
          "type": "Bool*",
          "default": "0"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "ValueType&",
      "docs": "!\nIf the value is not exist, it creates all parent values and a JSON Null value.\nSo it always succeed and return the newly created or existing value.\nRemind that it may change types of parents according to tokens, so it\npotentially removes previously stored values. For example, if a document\nwas an array, and \"/foo\" is used to create a value, then the document\nwill be changed to an object, and all existing array elements are lost.\n\\param root Root value of a DOM subtree to be resolved. It can be any value other than document root.\n\\param allocator Allocator for creating the values if the specified value or its parents are not exist.\n\\param alreadyExist If non-null, it stores whether the resolved value is already exist.\n\\return The resolved newly created (a JSON Null value), or already exists value."
    },
    {
      "id": "create-97fade",
      "name": "Create",
      "category": "pointer",
      "signature": "Create(Target, Document, Already Exist)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "GenericPointer*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Document",
          "type": "GenericDocument<EncodingType,ValueType::AllocatorType,stackAllocator>&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Already Exist",
          "type": "Bool*",
          "default": "0"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "template<stackAllocator> ValueType&",
      "docs": "!\n\\param document A document to be resolved.\n\\param alreadyExist If non-null, it stores whether the resolved value is already exist.\n\\return The resolved newly created, or already exists value."
    },
    {
      "id": "get-uri",
      "name": "GetUri",
      "category": "pointer",
      "signature": "GetUri(Target, Root, Root Uri, Unresolved Token Index, Allocator)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "GenericPointer*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Root",
          "type": "ValueType&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Root Uri",
          "type": "UriType&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Unresolved Token Index",
          "type": "size_t*",
          "default": "0"
        },
        {
          "name": "Allocator",
          "type": "Allocator*",
          "default": "0"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "UriType",
      "docs": "!\n\\param root Root value of a DOM sub-tree to be resolved. It can be any value other than document root.\n\\param rootUri Root URI\n\\param unresolvedTokenIndex If the pointer cannot resolve a token in the pointer, this parameter can obtain the index of unresolved token.\n\\param allocator Allocator for Uris\n\\return Uri if it can be resolved. Otherwise null.\n\\note\nThere are only 3 situations when a URI cannot be resolved:\n1. A value in the path is not an array nor object.\n2. An object value does not contain the token.\n3. A token is out of range of an array value.\nUse unresolvedTokenIndex to retrieve the token index."
    },
    {
      "id": "get",
      "name": "Get",
      "category": "pointer",
      "signature": "Get(Target, Root, Unresolved Token Index)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "GenericPointer*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Root",
          "type": "ValueType&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Unresolved Token Index",
          "type": "size_t*",
          "default": "0"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "ValueType*",
      "docs": "!\n\\param root Root value of a DOM sub-tree to be resolved. It can be any value other than document root.\n\\param unresolvedTokenIndex If the pointer cannot resolve a token in the pointer, this parameter can obtain the index of unresolved token.\n\\return Pointer to the value if it can be resolved. Otherwise null.\n\\note\nThere are only 3 situations when a value cannot be resolved:\n1. A value in the path is not an array nor object.\n2. An object value does not contain the token.\n3. A token is out of range of an array value.\nUse unresolvedTokenIndex to retrieve the token index."
    },
    {
      "id": "get-with-default-7f53ba",
      "name": "GetWithDefault",
      "category": "pointer",
      "signature": "GetWithDefault(Target, Root, Default Value, Allocator)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "GenericPointer*"
        },
